---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Brand from "../components/Brand.astro";
import { business } from "../data/business";
---

<Base title="Privacy policy">
  <header class="site-header legal-header wrap">
    <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Making Small Memories home">
      <Brand />
    </a>
    <a href="/">Back to the collection</a>
  </header>
  <main id="main" class="legal wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Your information matters</span>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>Effective date: May 30, 2026</p>
    <p>
      Making Small Memories is committed to protecting your privacy and
      safeguarding personal information shared through our website. This policy
      explains how we collect, use, disclose, and protect information when you
      visit our website, communicate with us, or use our services.
    </p>
    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p>
      We may collect information you voluntarily provide, including your name,
      phone number, email address, mailing address, insurance information,
      appointment or inquiry details, and information submitted through contact
      forms or scheduling systems.
    </p>
    <p>
      Certain information may be collected automatically, including your IP
      address, browser type, device information, pages visited, website usage
      data, and cookies or analytics information.
    </p>
    <h2>How we use your information</h2>
    <p>
      We may use your information to respond to inquiries, schedule
      appointments, provide services and related support, improve the website,
      communicate about services and scheduling, maintain business and legal
      records, and comply with applicable laws and regulations.
    </p>
    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Our website may link to scheduling systems, payment processors, social
      media platforms, and other external resources. We are not responsible for
      the privacy practices of third-party websites or services.
    </p>
    <h2>Data security and confidentiality</h2>
    <p>
      We implement reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards
      to protect information. No online transmission or storage system can be
      guaranteed completely secure.
    </p>
    <p>
      Communications through this website, standard email, or text messaging may
      not always be fully secure. Do not submit emergency, highly sensitive, or
      urgent medical or mental health information through website forms. If you
      are experiencing a medical or mental health emergency, call 911 or go to
      your nearest emergency room.
    </p>
    <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Our website is not intended for children under 13 without parental or
      guardian involvement.
    </p>
    <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      Our website may use cookies, analytics tools, and similar technologies to
      improve functionality and understand website usage. You may disable
      cookies through your browser settings.
    </p>
    <h2>Sharing information</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal information. We may share information when
      necessary with service providers assisting business operations, with
      insurance companies or healthcare entities when authorized, when required
      by law, or to protect the safety, rights, or property of clients, staff,
      or the public.
    </p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You may request access to your personal information, correction of
      inaccurate information, deletion of certain information where permitted by
      law, or withdrawal of consent for communications. Contact us using the
      details below.
    </p>
    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy at any time. Updates will be posted here with a
      revised effective date.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      {business.legalName}
      <br />
      <a href={`tel:${business.tel}`}>{business.phone}</a>
      <br />
      <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a>
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
